wn his message in a  new statement but his Holocaust remarks  have already strained German Palestinian  relations  I asked DW political correspondent Simon  young about the reactions this  controversial press conference has  spurred in Germany  yeah well this whole incident has  sparked a storm of reaction with even  for instance the normally reticent  former Chancellor Angela Merkel who  hasn't said much since he Lester left  office last year  condemning the remarks of the  Palestinian president but it's not just  about his remarks as you say it's also  about the uh slow reaction from  Chancellor Schultz and some people have  called that uh you know unprofessional  and there is this story that the  Chancellor's media advisor effectively  brought the press conference to an end  before the chancellor uh was about to  say something  um well you know that's fair enough but  I think the chancellor of Germany ought  to be responsible for his own actions uh  the uh leader of the opposition  Christian Democrat Party has called it  incomprehensible he says the that our  best should not just have been  contradicted he should have been told to  leave the chancellery rather than being  offered the handshake that uh Schultz  immediately thereafter did offer him and  there have been some negative comments  as well from Jewish leaders here and  other opposition politicians uh I think  uh you know you're seeing a lot of  aftermath a lot of broken porcelain uh  as they say on the floor and there's a  lot of repair work for the German  government to do they have summoned the  Palestinian representative in Berlin  today and told him of the government's  position on this yeah talking about  broken porcelain how do you think this  will affect german-palestinian relations  well some politicians are saying that  it's time to look again at the  development funding for the Palestinian  Authority more than a billion euros has  been promised from Germany we're making  it one of the biggest donors if not the  biggest some people are saying uh you  know Abbas is a uh supports terrorism  he's also a holocaust denier he's not  the sort of person who should be in  receipt of these uh kind of funds it's  fair to say in that press conference  Abbas was saying he hoped that  Chancellor Schultz would soon visit  Ramallah and the West Bank well the  Chancellor's press spokesman today was  saying it's very hard to imagine that  happening anytime in the foreseeable  future TW political correspondent Simon  young thanks so much
 

